## [Completed] May 31, 2026: Input Length and Format Validation in Feedback API (SEC-001)
- **Target File:** [functions/api/feedback.js](file:///H:/web3/gemini/website/functions/api/feedback.js)
- **Problem:** Lack of payload validation, format verification, and length bounds on input fields (`name`, `email`, `category`, `message`).
- **Remediation:**
  - Added strict parameter type and length validation: `message` (required, max 5000), `name` (optional, max 100), `email` (optional, max 100).
  - Whitelisted allowed `category` values to `['Bug Report', 'Feature Request', 'General Feedback']`.
  - Added regex checking for email format validation.
  - Returns `400 Bad Request` with structured error messages.
  - Sanitized database entry bindings with `.trim()`.

## [Completed] May 31, 2026: Dropdown Options Unreadability in Dark Mode
- **Target File:** [src/index.css](file:///H:/web3/gemini/website/src/index.css), [src/App.jsx](file:///H:/web3/gemini/website/src/App.jsx)
- **Problem:** In dark/light modes, native browser select option backgrounds and text colors did not dynamically scale, leading to low contrast and unreadable options.
- **Remediation:**
  - Added CSS definitions for `.theme-select` and `.theme-select option`.
  - Forced option background color to `var(--bg-dark)` and text color to `var(--text-main)` with `!important` to override native OS/browser controls.
  - Cleaned up inline select styles in `src/App.jsx` to rely entirely on stylesheet class definitions.
